    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. The range of arctan is (-\\pi/2,\\pi/2), giving the selected range values. For both point questions, points I and II satisfy x=tan(y) with y in that interval, while III fails. The complex quotient simplifies to \\sqrt{3}/2+\\text{i}/2, with magnitude 1 and argument \\pi/6. Substitution u=4+x^6 gives the first integral as (4+x^6)^6/18+C; substitution u=x^2+2x gives the second as ln|x^2+2x|+C. Principal inverse trigonometric values give 3\\pi/4, 2\\pi/3, and -2\\pi/3. For the vector questions, cos(theta) equals 19/\\sqrt{1961}, 2/\\sqrt{754}, 1/\\sqrt{182}, -1, -5/\\sqrt{399}, and -1/\\sqrt{5}, respectively, producing the stated rounded angles. In q-101510, PR=-2PQ, so the angle is exactly 180 degrees. The dot-product constraints give t=1 in q-19038 and t=2 in q-101514. Evidence below comes from worked solutions, not captured grades.",
